-- Summary of tamper experiments:
-- TA: system: trusts whatever is IN the OS bundle; replacing it with a self-built CA
--     makes self-signed (by that CA) certs pass; real-public sites then fail (real roots gone).
-- TB: with mTLS (server requires client cert), bundle content decides crash vs graceful:
--     ANY private key block in bundle -> CRASH (ORA-03113); no key -> graceful ORA-29259.
-- TC: appended to the real 148-root bundle, ANY non-CERTIFICATE block (RSA/EC/PKCS8 private
--     key, CSR, PKCS7) OR binary data -> CRASH; plain non-PEM text -> ignored (OK).
-- Conclusion: system:'s bundle loader is not tolerant -- the OS CA bundle must contain ONLY
--     CERTIFICATE PEM blocks (+ ignorable text); any other content crashes the dedicated server.
